# Implementation Plan - Simple Multiplayer "Micro Football" Game

Create a lightweight, high-performance multiplayer football game with jumping, 5-minute sessions, and 1-minute cooldowns.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This project requires **Node.js** installed on the system.
> The game will run on a local server (default port 3000).

## Proposed Changes

### [micro-football] Project Structure

#### [NEW] [package.json](file:///d:/Gigmos%20Solution/OneDrive%20-%20Gigmo%20Solutions%20Pvt%20Ltd/ashu-gairola/gigmos_testing_ground/micro-football/package.json)
Initialize Node project with `express` and `socket.io`.

#### [NEW] [server.js](file:///d:/Gigmos%20Solution/OneDrive%20-%20Gigmo%20Solutions%20Pvt%20Ltd/ashu-gairola/gigmos_testing_ground/micro-football/server.js)
Setup the Express server and handle Socket.io connections.
- **High-performance heartbeat**: Update loop at 60Hz for fluid movement.
- **Session Manager**: Track a 5-minute "Game On" period followed by a 1-minute "Cooldown".
- **Physics Engine**: Manage ball position, player teams, and goal detection.

#### [NEW] [public/index.html](file:///d:/Gigmos%20Solution/OneDrive%20-%20Gigmo%20Solutions%20Pvt%20Ltd/ashu-gairola/gigmos_testing_ground/micro-football/public/index.html)
The game's entry point with a login screen and gameplay canvas.

#### [NEW] [public/style.css](file:///d:/Gigmos%20Solution/OneDrive%20-%20Gigmo%20Solutions%20Pvt%20Ltd/ashu-gairola/gigmos_testing_ground/micro-football/public/style.css)
Modern, "WOW" aesthetics with a pitch-themed design and glassmorphism.

#### [NEW] [public/game.js](file:///d:/Gigmos%20Solution/OneDrive%20-%20Gigmo%20Solutions%20Pvt%20Ltd/ashu-gairola/gigmos_testing_ground/micro-football/public/game.js)
Frontend logic for rendering the field, ball, and players.
- **Jumping**: Implement `z` or `height` coordinate for players and ball.
- **Client-side Prediction**: Ensure movement feels instant for the user.
- **UI Overlay**: Show session timer and score.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No automated tests for this simple POC, but I will verify the build and server startup.

### Manual Verification
1. Run `npm install` and `node server.js`.
2. Open `http://localhost:3000` in multiple browser tabs.
3. Verify that players are assigned to Red and Blue teams alternately.
4. Verify that players can move the ball by "collision" (walking into it).
5. Verify that scoring a goal updates the score for everyone.
6. Verify that closing a tab removes the player.
